WEBVTT

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:15.521
SYNDROME: (BARELY AUDIBLE)
Most important,
keep things light.

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:19.521
Praise him.
Make him feel like we
appreciate his abilities.

00:00:20.841 --> 00:00:22.121
Am I overdressed?

00:00:22.201 --> 00:00:24.801
Actually,
you look rather dashing.

00:00:25.641 --> 00:00:27.961
BOB: I take it
our host is...
MIRAGE: I'm sorry.

00:00:28.041 --> 00:00:31.201
He won't be dining with us.
He hopes you'll understand.

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:35.081
Of course. I do usually
make it a point to know
who I'm working for.

00:00:35.161 --> 00:00:38.121
He prefers a certain
amount of anonymity.

00:00:38.201 --> 00:00:40.521
Surely,
you of all people
understand that.

00:00:40.681 --> 00:00:45.281
I was just wondering,
of all the places to
settle down, why live...

00:00:45.401 --> 00:00:48.481
With a volcano?
He's attracted
to power.

00:00:48.561 --> 00:00:49.721
So am I.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.641
It's a weakness
we share.

00:00:51.961 --> 00:00:53.561
Seems a bit unstable.

00:00:53.681 --> 00:00:56.881
I prefer to think of it
as misunderstood.

00:00:57.481 --> 00:00:58.481
(CHUCKLING)
Aren't we all?

00:00:58.561 --> 00:01:01.321
Volcanic soil is among
the most fertile on Earth.

00:01:01.401 --> 00:01:04.481
Everything at the table
was grown right here.

00:01:04.561 --> 00:01:06.641
How does it compare?

00:01:06.721 --> 00:01:08.921
Everything's delicious.

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:32.921
Jeez.

00:02:33.001 --> 00:02:34.001
HELEN:
Hurry, honey.

00:02:34.081 --> 00:02:36.361
Or you'll be
late for work.

00:02:38.201 --> 00:02:39.841
Have a great day, honey.
Thanks.

00:02:39.961 --> 00:02:41.761
Help customers,
climb ladders...

00:02:41.841 --> 00:02:42.841
Bring bacon.

00:02:42.921 --> 00:02:44.961
All that jazz.

00:02:45.321 --> 00:02:46.681
(LAUGHING)

00:02:52.841 --> 00:02:53.921
You have an appointment?

00:02:54.001 --> 00:02:55.841
I'm an old friend.
I just wanted to...

00:02:55.961 --> 00:02:57.761
All visitors
are required...

00:02:57.841 --> 00:02:59.841
E: Go check
the electric fence.

00:02:59.961 --> 00:03:02.001
What is it?
Who are you?
What do you want?

00:03:03.841 --> 00:03:07.321
My God, you've gotten fat.
Come in. Come, come.

00:03:14.841 --> 00:03:17.361
Yes, things are
going quite well.

00:03:17.441 --> 00:03:19.281
Quite well.
My God, no complaints.

00:03:19.361 --> 00:03:23.641
But, you know,
it is not the same.
Not the same at all.

00:03:23.721 --> 00:03:26.521
Weren't you in the news?
Some show in Prayge...
Prague?

00:03:26.681 --> 00:03:28.961
Milan, darling. Milan.

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:33.001
Supermodels.
Nothing super about them.

00:03:33.081 --> 00:03:35.321
Spoiled, stupid,
little stick figures

00:03:35.401 --> 00:03:37.881
with poofy lips
who think only
about themselves.

00:03:38.001 --> 00:03:41.881
Feh! I used to
design for gods.

00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:45.641
But perhaps you come
with a challenge, eh?

00:03:45.721 --> 00:03:48.121
I was surprised
to get your call.

00:03:48.201 --> 00:03:50.481
E, I just need
a patch job.

00:03:50.561 --> 00:03:53.881
Hmm. This is megamesh.
Outmoded, but very sturdy.

00:03:54.001 --> 00:03:56.161
And you've torn
right through it!

00:03:56.241 --> 00:03:58.481
What have you
been doing, Robert?

00:03:58.561 --> 00:04:01.161
Moonlighting hero work?

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:03.121
Must have happened
a long time ago.

00:04:03.201 --> 00:04:06.201
I see. This is
a hobo suit, darling.

00:04:06.281 --> 00:04:08.841
You can't be seen in this.
I won't allow it!

00:04:08.921 --> 00:04:11.681
Fifteen years ago,
maybe, but now?

00:04:11.761 --> 00:04:13.081
What do you mean?
You designed it.

00:04:13.161 --> 00:04:16.281
I never look back, darling.
It distracts from the now.

00:04:16.361 --> 00:04:19.001
You need a new suit.
That much is certain.

00:04:19.081 --> 00:04:21.521
A new suit? Where the heck
am I gonna get a new suit?

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:24.081
You can't!
It's impossible!
I'm far too busy.

00:04:24.201 --> 00:04:26.361
So ask me now,
before I again
become sane.

00:04:26.441 --> 00:04:29.361
Wait. You want
to make me a suit?

00:04:29.441 --> 00:04:32.761
You push too hard,
darling! But I accept.

00:04:33.481 --> 00:04:35.881
It will be bold.
Dramatic!
Yeah.

00:04:35.961 --> 00:04:37.201
Heroic!

00:04:37.281 --> 00:04:40.961
Yeah, something classic,
like Dynaguy!

00:04:41.041 --> 00:04:44.681
Oh! He had a great look!
Oh, the cape and the boots...

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:45.801
No capes!

00:04:46.961 --> 00:04:48.361
Isn't that
my decision?

00:04:48.441 --> 00:04:50.961
Do you remember
Thunderhead?

00:04:51.081 --> 00:04:52.561
Tall, storm powers.

00:04:52.641 --> 00:04:53.801
Nice man.
Good with kids.

00:04:53.921 --> 00:04:54.881
Listen, E...

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:57.201
November 15th of '58.

00:04:58.641 --> 00:05:00.721
All was well,
another day saved

00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:03.641
when his cape snagged
on a missile fin.

00:05:03.721 --> 00:05:06.041
Thunderhead was not
the brightest bulb...

00:05:06.121 --> 00:05:07.161
Stratogale!

00:05:07.241 --> 00:05:12.521
April 23rd, '57.
Cape caught in
a jet turbine.

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:14.881
You can't generalize
about these things.

00:05:15.001 --> 00:05:18.241
Meta-Man. Express elevator.
Dynaguy, snag on takeoff.

00:05:18.321 --> 00:05:22.161
Splashdown,
sucked into a vortex.
No capes!

00:05:22.241 --> 00:05:23.281
Now, go on.

00:05:23.481 --> 00:05:25.641
Your new suit will be
finished before your
next assignment.

00:05:25.721 --> 00:05:27.761
You know I'm retired
from hero work.

00:05:27.841 --> 00:05:31.081
As am I, Robert.
Yet, here we are.

00:05:31.161 --> 00:05:35.561
E, I only need a patch job.
For sentimental reasons.

00:05:36.361 --> 00:05:39.681
(SIGHS) Fine.
I will also fix
the hobo suit.

00:05:40.521 --> 00:05:42.281
You're the best
of the best, E.

00:05:42.361 --> 00:05:44.641
Yes, I know, darling.
I know.

00:05:54.041 --> 00:05:56.401
(PHONE RINGS)

00:05:57.801 --> 00:05:59.681
BOB: Don't answer it,
honey, I got it!

00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:00.841
Hello?

00:06:01.001 --> 00:06:02.521
We have a new
assignment for you.

00:06:06.961 --> 00:06:08.201
MIRAGE: How soon
can you get here?

00:06:08.281 --> 00:06:09.481
BOB: I'll leave
tomorrow morning.

00:06:09.641 --> 00:06:12.441
MIRAGE: See you there.
Goodbye.

00:06:14.161 --> 00:06:16.881
Who was that, honey?
The, uh, office?

00:06:16.961 --> 00:06:19.881
Another conference.
Short notice, but,
you know,

00:06:19.961 --> 00:06:21.801
duty calls.
(NERVOUS LAUGH)

00:06:29.681 --> 00:06:31.641
HELEN: Bob?
Yeah, what's up, honey?

00:06:33.561 --> 00:06:35.081
Ha... Have a great trip.

00:06:35.201 --> 00:06:36.201
Thanks, sweetie.

00:06:36.281 --> 00:06:37.561
I'll call you
when I get there.

00:06:37.641 --> 00:06:38.801
I love you.

00:06:38.921 --> 00:06:40.521
So much.

00:06:41.721 --> 00:06:43.081
I love you, too.

00:06:56.241 --> 00:06:58.201
SHIP'S COMPUTER:
This is your
automated Captain.

00:06:58.281 --> 00:07:01.521
Would you care
for more mimosa?

00:07:01.601 --> 00:07:03.201
Don't mind if I do.
Thanks.

00:07:03.281 --> 00:07:04.761
You're welcome.

00:07:06.401 --> 00:07:09.081
Currently 78 degrees
in Nomanisan.

00:07:09.161 --> 00:07:11.041
Perfect weather
for flying.

00:07:17.001 --> 00:07:18.561
Please fasten
your seat belt.

00:07:18.641 --> 00:07:20.761
We're beginning
our descent.

